qreplace(n,9,'workedExample','Remaining options for the defender: block the CDN wholesale, control DNS so HTTPS records are not delivered, use managed-endpoint filtering, or intercept TLS, each with its own costs.','Visibility and enforcement depend on deployment. Managed-endpoint policy can provide a different control point; DNS manipulation does not guarantee a silent downgrade of a client already attempting authenticated ECH.','ECHdowngraderesistanceandnoeasyinterceptguarantee.',ech)
